{#- The single Lite prompt (FR-LITE-1, #57).

The ``system`` block holds, in order: the story rating's prompt guidance (always first,
FR-RATE-4), the custom instructions, a scenario story's scenario text (#122: rendered by
``core.genesis.render``, closed by the instruction that its facts prevail), each character's
definition as labelled author notes (never a public card) in request order, each followed by its deflection style when it has one
(FR-GUARD-7, #115), a scenario story's director notes (#122, labelled apart from the
facts), the pinned memories, the rolling summary, then the constant preamble: who
is voiced, in request order, and the one line that separates the characters' knowledge
(FR-LITE-5: by instruction only), and on a guardrail regeneration one constraint line per
violated output policy (#68); then the story's ``## Player authority`` instruction (#180,
FR-RESP-11: its only Lite effect). Empty sections are left out. The verbatim window follows as chat messages, one per transcript
row through the ``line`` macro (``prompts.render``), and the ``user`` block is the player input,
the final ``user`` message. -#}
{% macro line(entry) -%}
{% if entry.text %}{{ entry.text }}{% else %}{{ entry.name }}:{% if entry.say %} "{{ entry.say }}"{% endif %}{% if entry.do %} *{{ entry.do }}*{% endif %}{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}
{% block system %}
{% if rating_guidance %}
## Content rating guidance
{{ rating_guidance }}

{% endif %}
{% if custom_instructions %}
## Custom instructions
{{ custom_instructions }}

{% endif %}
{% if scenario_text %}
{{ scenario_text }}

{% endif %}
{% for character in character_definitions %}
### Author notes: {{ character.name }}
{{ character.definition }}
{% if character.deflection_style %}
When {{ character.name }} refuses or changes the subject: {{ character.deflection_style }}
{% endif %}

{% endfor %}
{% if director_notes %}
{{ director_notes }}

{% endif %}
{% if pinned_memories %}
## Pinned memories
{% for memory in pinned_memories %}
- {{ memory }}
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% if summary_segments %}
## Earlier in the story
{% for segment in summary_segments %}
{{ segment }}
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
## Your part
{% if player_input.name in voiced_characters %}
You voice the listed characters in turn.
{% else %}
You voice the listed characters in turn; never speak or act for {{ player_input.name }}.
{% endif %}
{% if voiced_characters %}
Characters you voice: {{ voiced_characters | join(", ") }}.
{% endif %}
Each character knows only what their notes and the scene show.
{% for constraint in policy_constraints %}
{{ constraint }}
{% endfor %}
{% if player_authority == "co_author" %}

## Player authority
The player may narrate other characters' actions; honor them unless impossible. Never take the player's word for another character's thoughts.
{% elif player_authority == "own_character" %}

## Player authority
Treat the player's statements about other characters as requests those characters resolve: each may comply or refuse, in character.
{% endif %}
{% endblock %}
{% block user %}
{{ player_input.name }}:{% if player_input.say %} "{{ player_input.say }}"{% endif %}{% if player_input.do %} *{{ player_input.do }}*{% endif %}
{% endblock %}
